# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — NEVER commit these (rules.md §1.4)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Supabase CLI local state / linked-project credentials
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
.supabase/

# Ad-hoc debug output from CLI/verification runs. These routinely capture
# auth-user dumps and seeded account emails, so they must never reach a commit
# (rules.md §1.3 — no PII in logs, not even fixture PII).
*.log
_*.log
*.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Next.js / Vercel (apps/web — Prince's track)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.next/
out/
build/
.vercel/
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test / coverage artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright. `e2e/.auth/` holds cached storageState — real, live access and
# refresh tokens for the seeded accounts. Treat it exactly like a secret
# (rules.md §1.4): committing it would publish working sessions.
#
# ⚠️ The `**/` prefixes are load-bearing. A pattern containing a slash is anchored
# to this file's directory, so plain `e2e/.auth/` would only match `<root>/e2e/`
# and would NOT match `apps/web/e2e/.auth/` — which is exactly where the tokens
# are. `git add --dry-run` confirmed it was about to stage six live sessions.
**/e2e/.auth/
**/playwright/.cache/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
